new monuments are now on display not too  far from downtown city leaders adding  them as a way to honor historic las  vegas historic west side community you  can find them  on the on and off ramps at u.s 95 at mlk  8 news now reporter madison kimbrough  live tonight with an up close  and personal look madison  yes brian take a look at this monument  sign it is very visible right as you get  off of 95.  local artist harold bradford says he  wanted to create a sense of community  with this piece back in the day the  historic west side of las vegas  was home to mostly african americans and  their businesses  the rich culture that took place on the  west side has never been forgotten  and now with these signs in present day  this is just one way the city hopes to  revitalize the area  well as a person that grew up in the  historic west side and still lives in  historic wayside  there's a sense of pride that we all  have there's some something  within that design that they they  perhaps feel that they can hold on to  and that was my concern also and i had  you know all that in mind as  as i started my designs  and the sign on the north side of the  u.s 95 off-ramp is not completely  finished yet  but will have a four foot wide walking  path allowing people to come  up and take pictures now if you look  really closely you'll notice that the  design  is in the shape of a compass and that  star you see  that is supposed to represent the west  side it is a beautiful  monument that we see right here great  way to represent  this historic area reporting live  madison kimbrough  8 news now
 

